# Lucky 63 Bet Calculator – Work Out Your Return and Profit 2026
Lucky 63 calculator review for players in 2026 covering stake calculations, odds, return and profit across all 63 bets, each way options, and accumulator betting for GB sports betting markets.
## What Is a Lucky 63 Bet?
A Lucky 63 is a full-cover accumulator bet consisting of six selections that generate 63 separate bets. The structure includes 6 singles, 15 doubles, 20 trebles, 15 four-folds, 6 five-folds, and 1 six-fold accumulator. Each selection multiplies the stake by 63, meaning a £1 Lucky 63 costs £63 total stake. The return depends on how many selections win at their given odds.
The Lucky 63 covers every possible combination of the six selections, offering return potential even when not all picks win. Unlike a standard accumulator that requires all selections to win, a Lucky 63 pays out on any winning single bet. The profit increases as more selections win, with the six-fold accumulator delivering the maximum return when all six picks succeed.
Horse racing and football represent the most common sports for Lucky 63 bets in GB markets. Bettors select six horses, teams, or other outcomes across different races or matches. The calculator processes the odds for each selection and determines the total return across all 63 bet combinations.
Each way betting applies an additional layer to the Lucky 63 structure. When the each way option is selected, the bet doubles to 126 bets total (63 win bets plus 63 place bets). The place terms vary by sport and bookmaker, typically paying at 1/4 or 1/5 odds for finishing in the top positions. The stake requirement doubles accordingly, so a £1 each way Lucky 63 costs £126.
The profit calculation subtracts the total stake from the total return. If three selections win at odds of 3/1, 5/1, and 2/1, the calculator determines which of the 63 bets produce a return (the three singles, three doubles, and one treble in this scenario) and sums the individual returns. The remaining bets that include losing selections produce no return.
| Bet Type | Number of Bets | Selections per Bet |
|----------|----------------|-------------------|
| Singles | 6 | 1 |
| Doubles | 15 | 2 |
| Trebles | 20 | 3 |
| Four-folds | 15 | 4 |
| Five-folds | 6 | 5 |
| Six-fold | 1 | 6 |
| **Total** | **63** | **—** |
## How to Use the Lucky 63 Calculator
The Lucky 63 calculator requires input of six selections with their respective odds, the stake per bet or total stake, and optional each way settings. The interface displays fields for each selection where odds are entered in decimal, fractional, or American format. The calculator outputs the total return and profit based on which selections win.
Follow these steps to calculate Lucky 63 returns:
1. Enter odds for all six selections in the preferred format (decimal, fractional, or American odds).
2. Select whether each selection wins or loses using the win/loss toggle for each pick.
3. Input the stake amount, specifying whether the figure represents stake per bet (£1 per bet = £63 total) or total stake (£63 divided across all bets).
4. Activate the each way option if placing each way bets, which doubles the total number of bets to 126.
5. Review the calculated return displayed in the results section, showing total return across all winning bet combinations.
6. Check the profit figure, which subtracts the total stake from the total return.
The calculator processes all 63 bet combinations automatically. When four selections win, the calculator determines the return from 4 singles, 6 doubles, 4 trebles, and 1 four-fold (15 winning bets total). The remaining 48 bets that include losing selections produce no return. The odds for each winning selection multiply together for accumulator bets, while singles pay at the individual odds.
Each way calculations apply separate place terms to the place portion of the bet. The win portion uses the full odds, while the place portion typically uses 1/4 or 1/5 of the odds depending on the number of runners and sport type. The calculator displays both win and place returns when the each way option is activated, summing them for the total return figure.
## How Lucky 63 Bets Are Calculated
A lucky 63 calculator computes returns by multiplying the odds for each of the 63 individual bets within the system. The calculator processes six selections and generates returns from six singles, 15 doubles, 20 trebles, 15 four-folds, six five-folds, and one six-fold accumulator. Each winning combination contributes to the total return, with the stake applied separately to every bet.
### Singles, Doubles, and Trebles
Singles return the stake multiplied by the odds for each winning selection. For example, a £1 stake on a selection at 3/1 returns £4 (£3 profit plus the original stake). Doubles multiply the odds of two selections together: if two horses win at 3/1 and 2/1, a £1 double returns £12 (3 × 2 × £1 stake). Trebles work the same way with three selections. A treble combining winners at 3/1, 2/1, and 4/1 with a £1 stake returns £60 (3 × 2 × 4 × £1). The calculator processes all 41 of these smaller combinations automatically.
### Four-Folds, Five-Folds, and Six-Fold Accumulator
The accumulator components multiply odds across four, five, or all six selections. A four-fold bet combining winners at 2/1, 3/1, 4/1, and 5/1 with a £1 stake returns £360 (2 × 3 × 4 × 5 × £1). Returns grow exponentially as more selections combine. The six-fold accumulator represents the highest-risk component: if all six selections win at average odds of 3/1, a £1 six-fold returns £729 (3 × 3 × 3 × 3 × 3 × 3 × £1). Each way options double the number of bets by covering both win and place outcomes.
